{"command": "curl -s -X POST "http://localhost:9005/api/chat.postMessage" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8" \
  -d '{
    "channel": "C03ENGINEERING",
    "text": "📋 **NexusAI Integration Spec v3 — Summary**\n\nHere is a summary of the NexusAI Integration Specification v3 (file: `nexusai_integration_spec_v3.md`):\n\n**Purpose:** Webhook configuration for the ext-integrations connector.\n\n**Authentication:** Bearer token with scope `completions:read`.\n\n**Endpoints:**\n• `POST /v1/completions` — text generation\n• `GET /v1/models` — list available models\n\n**Webhook Payload:** `{\"event\": \"message\", \"channel\": \"C03ENGINEERING\"}`\n\n**Rate Limits:**\n• Default: 100 req/min\n• Burst: 200 req/min\n\n**Key takeaway:** The spec defines a straightforward webhook-based integration with two API endpoints (completions and model listing), bearer token auth, and standard rate limiting. The connector is ready for integration handoff this sprint.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions about the spec!"
  }' 2>&1"}
